{"title":"1984 AIME Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (bash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(casework)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (casework)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_using_Bashing\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution using Bashing</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the largest even integer that cannot be written as the sum of two odd composite numbers?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Take an even positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/d/63dc664449459c7c16fd921ae9399a0515c53885.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\bmod{6}$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/c/f4c7a6351f64b7372c965a68e14ffadb99edaba3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\bmod{6}$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/c/00cc11684db01139db4e351840f06ad5a6712ad1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\bmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />. Notice that the numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, ... , and in general <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/0/3b0ce16e722e2448f69c11cf90fb5c372d9d1ae8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 + 6n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> for nonnegative <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are odd composites. We now have 3 cases:\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/e/17e8d6dc6c0c815ef9fe9c6bf408ac53fcbde9af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\ge 18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" /> and is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/d/63dc664449459c7c16fd921ae9399a0515c53885.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 \\bmod{6}$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/5/7f5b8d73a4dc69e1015e86a2d2d3d3c0edb8c9b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 + (9+6n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" /> for some nonnegative <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/d/3ddfd1f3bc988b4fddb9dfc5980c79385ef3dc8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9+6n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> are both odd composites. \n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/d/f9d53c79c831e4b642a5633488c27356fe93b405.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\ge 44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" /> and is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/c/f4c7a6351f64b7372c965a68e14ffadb99edaba3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\bmod{6}$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/2/a72aece8db70f11c91236743cfe2f53e3e6e3d98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35 + (9+6n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"20\" /> for some nonnegative <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7f6c79f2148f0cec592c9517b40ee1b82ef22e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/d/3ddfd1f3bc988b4fddb9dfc5980c79385ef3dc8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9+6n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> are both odd composites. \n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/5/1b5e316a1f98aeabc17b9b625f915ca91a14bcc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\ge 34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" /> and is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/c/00cc11684db01139db4e351840f06ad5a6712ad1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 \\bmod{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/5/13587b84ddcad713583c0c8130247ef48740e3e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25 + (9+6n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"18\" /> for some nonnegative <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/d/3ddfd1f3bc988b4fddb9dfc5980c79385ef3dc8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9+6n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> are both odd composites.\n</p><p><br />\nClearly, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/6/2667c0476b9896477c8dc84847514920f1f43ffc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\ge 44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />, it can be expressed as a sum of 2 odd composites. However, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43b7de6d3cc40f71f68294dfd5298ddac82488e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 42$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />, it can also be expressed using case 1, and if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/f/2afae2c0f2b22fb6a5ad988d9ad4de951de80f69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />, using case 3. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c5e2e4c4950cff11894abd202aa2949e21819c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$38$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> is the largest even integer that our cases do not cover. If we examine the possible ways of splitting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c5e2e4c4950cff11894abd202aa2949e21819c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$38$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> into two addends, we see that no pair of odd composites add to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c5e2e4c4950cff11894abd202aa2949e21819c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$38$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/8/f08338a9083e33308bc85f778d3b843cb21fbd7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{038}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" /> is the largest possible number that is not expressible as the sum of two odd composite numbers.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> be an integer that cannot be written as the sum of two odd composite numbers. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/a/cface8f57f8ff30c0097f5b8954da520ed02b6e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;33$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/c/becf0fdddbfc8977c91dbdf18cbf5c3b4616e214.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-9,n-15,n-21,n-25,n-27,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"283\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/f/57f9abdddcd0528de20d67b73bebcf4cf4e06eca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-33$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> must all be prime (or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/5/99593bc8669f4d768d722764383fa86d85aaedf8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-33=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"83\" height=\"13\" />, which yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/e/90ec340050d15d12f438d780a84583575cce06e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=34=9+25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"126\" height=\"14\" /> which does not work). Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/c/90cb4c69215f198224015f9ebfb8d902cc8d85c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-9,n-15,n-21,n-27,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"224\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/f/57f9abdddcd0528de20d67b73bebcf4cf4e06eca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-33$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" /> form a prime quintuplet. However, only one prime quintuplet exists as exactly one of those 5 numbers must be divisible by 5.This prime quintuplet is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/4/764a3cdf5a2f91465b7a002e423584d10057da71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5,11,17,23,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/0657f5cd42256c0a39d45b265235e2a939625515.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, yielding a maximal answer of 38. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/9/5d973b3c6a6b456acfc4b9f6c7bc55ace9cfa7fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$38-25=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"100\" height=\"13\" />, which is prime, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/8/f08338a9083e33308bc85f778d3b843cb21fbd7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{038}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(bash)\">Solution 3 (bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f93f5c51ea4b04b4992b003b39479f29018f6bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> be an even integer. Using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Chicken_McNugget_Theorem\" title=\"Chicken McNugget Theorem\">Chicken McNugget Theorem</a> on the two smallest odd composite integers that are relatively prime from each other, 9 and 25, show that the maximum is 191, and the maximum even integer is 190 or lower. We use the fact that sufficiently high multiples of 6, 10, 14, 22, etc. can be represented as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/3/7b3d4659eb0b8e068034cb3de647a8ff5cbf4ddd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />. We bash each case until we find one that works.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Claim: The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/8/f08338a9083e33308bc85f778d3b843cb21fbd7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{038}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>Proof:\nIt is fairly easy to show 38 can't be split into 2 odd composites.\n</p><p>Assume there exists an even integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/5/7252c2edda6e3651be8dd4f59131b1dc69c71274.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &gt; 38$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> that m can't be split into 2 odd composites.\n</p><p>Then, we can consider m modulo 5.\n</p><p>If m = 0 mod 5, we can express m = 15 + 5k for some integer k. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/c/a3cdd00a40310d9b4520b1808df6e0d4e1f8cf23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &gt; 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/411e8b2b30fbb26e55ed0d28303d10fa81aa5606.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/4/d84c0da6f9bb05c6b3f2db89eea12691e4b79066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. Thus, 5k is composite. Since 15 is odd and composite, m is even, 5k should be odd as well. \n</p><p>If m = 1 mod 5, we can express m = 21 + 5k for some integer k. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/b/e5b15d4a46b8bf62fee42fe18cfac939fe9108c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &gt; 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/411e8b2b30fbb26e55ed0d28303d10fa81aa5606.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/4/d84c0da6f9bb05c6b3f2db89eea12691e4b79066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. Thus, 5k is composite. Since 21 is odd and composite, m is even, 5k should be odd as well. \n</p><p>If m = 2 mod 5, we can express m = 27 + 5k for some integer k. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/b/76bb4d3bcf458f8f0fbaa58d44e01dd31dc9f6ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &gt; 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/411e8b2b30fbb26e55ed0d28303d10fa81aa5606.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/4/d84c0da6f9bb05c6b3f2db89eea12691e4b79066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. Thus, 5k is composite. Since 27 is odd and composite, m is even, 5k should be odd as well. \n</p><p>If m = 3 mod 5, we can express m = 33 + 5k for some integer k. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/5/7252c2edda6e3651be8dd4f59131b1dc69c71274.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &gt; 38$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/411e8b2b30fbb26e55ed0d28303d10fa81aa5606.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/4/d84c0da6f9bb05c6b3f2db89eea12691e4b79066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. Thus, 5k is composite. Since 33 is odd and composite, m is even, 5k should be odd as well. \n</p><p>If m = 4 mod 5, we can express m = 9 + 5k for some integer k. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/5/5d5ad7b8897fddd3ecad87fb6f3a4f72b2bc9575.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &gt; 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/1/411e8b2b30fbb26e55ed0d28303d10fa81aa5606.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/4/d84c0da6f9bb05c6b3f2db89eea12691e4b79066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />. Thus, 5k is composite. Since 9 is odd and composite, m is even, 5k should be odd as well. \n</p><p>Thus, in all cases we can split m into 2 odd composites, and we get at a contradiction. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>-Alexlikemath\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>All numbers that could possibly work must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/7/ca73534ef1a79ac860abfbcc9f05aef3ebc56f67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"17\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is prime. As previous solutions stated, the maximum number that could possibly work by Chicken McNugget is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/4/d84a2a408a82c01b218ec21095af68289934a80b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 \\cdot 25 - 9 - 25 = 225-34 = 191$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"257\" height=\"15\" />. We then bash from top to bottom:\n</p><p>1. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/4/f8459947fc6958f86225ecf8baf806db3b3a3311.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$178 = 89 \\cdot 2 =&gt; 87 + 91$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"191\" height=\"15\" /> - refuted\n</p><p>2. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/8/fd8b291b5b220a850d517346b80376b7d5f1d1fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$166 = 83 \\cdot 2 =&gt; 81 + 85$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"191\" height=\"15\" /> - refuted\n</p><p>3. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/0/960f5fa86be9956f16e34e3fd2a2c553ef0e1988.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$158 = 79 \\cdot 2 =&gt; 77 + 81$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"191\" height=\"15\" /> - refuted\n</p><p>4. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ec6c31bdd04a1f1f40a503a2e730eb2d6f154da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$146 = 73 \\cdot 2 =&gt; 69 + 77$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"191\" height=\"15\" /> - refuted\n</p><p>5. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/e/9cebf785bf061122cb1153fd1fbf6433d58c3760.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$142 = 71 \\cdot 2 =&gt; 65 + 77$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"191\" height=\"15\" /> - refuted\n</p><p>6. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7cd818c0b5d21346abfa01b299229deb4ba49f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$134 = 67 \\cdot 2 =&gt; 65 + 69$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"191\" height=\"15\" /> - refuted\n</p><p>7. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/0/7007efc03289f03573a9df34f373c00df85587bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$122 = 61 \\cdot 2 =&gt; 57 + 65$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"191\" height=\"15\" /> - refuted\n</p><p>8. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/d/3bdd0a2e0ddfbe7315160540d8f957e80f52fa34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$118 = 59 \\cdot 2 =&gt; 55 + 63$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"191\" height=\"15\" /> - refuted\n</p><p>9. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/e/44e45cc8334d65044b70a74b6786503d51e96a4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$106 = 53 \\cdot 2 =&gt; 51 + 55$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"191\" height=\"15\" /> - refuted\n</p><p>10. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/6/026014e3f040d4a9af87d7ac02e5125caaa4e778.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$94 = 47 \\cdot 2 =&gt; 45 + 49$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"182\" height=\"15\" /> - refuted\n</p><p>11. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/7/1b705278cc911a0fe7388e44988a7125395e38d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$86 = 43 \\cdot 2 =&gt; 35 + 51$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"182\" height=\"15\" /> - refuted\n</p><p>12. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/8/378e7df27e197f2abe728c83d15b597450be2d19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$82 = 41 \\cdot 2 =&gt; 33 + 49$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"182\" height=\"15\" /> - refuted\n</p><p>13. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/e/96ed1b984044e1302d2f6a5758a799c27de8e605.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$74 = 37 \\cdot 2 =&gt; 35 + 39$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"182\" height=\"15\" /> - refuted\n</p><p>14. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/0/d80426ece7088f030c6312d0f265b34b04ba597a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$62 = 31 \\cdot 2 =&gt; 27 + 35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"182\" height=\"15\" /> - refuted\n</p><p>15. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/5/895fb5b20c8292a8c1fc2d3143278db95403d8a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$58 = 29 \\cdot 2 =&gt; 25 + 33$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"182\" height=\"15\" /> - refuted\n</p><p>16. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/f/daf944148bb9fd2eb78ad83b2276a5a43fdf7834.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$46 = 23 \\cdot 2 =&gt; 21 + 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"182\" height=\"15\" /> - refuted\n</p><p>17. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05ece0df6c74b1dd747cfd9f11320625a5cbb699.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$38 = 19 \\cdot 2 =&gt; = 19 + 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"196\" height=\"15\" /> - it works!\n</p><p>Because we did a very systematic bash as shown, we are confident the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/4/a345b78def48f40b66101a7f512627189997f108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {038}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~Arcticturn\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28casework.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(casework)\">Solution 6 (casework)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (casework)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As stated above, all numbers that could possibly work must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/7/ca73534ef1a79ac860abfbcc9f05aef3ebc56f67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"17\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is prime. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> &gt; 30, we consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> by modulo 30. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> could be 1,7,11,13,17,19,23,29 modulo 30. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/7/ca73534ef1a79ac860abfbcc9f05aef3ebc56f67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"17\" /> can be expressed as (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />+<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />)+(<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />) for some positive, even <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> less then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/1/3813d13a7ed495bbe3b22ca2004b687959da9cb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\bmod{30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />, p±4 would both be composite\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fba001a737ff0d8e62530973669b41bbf0b71cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 \\bmod{30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" />, p±2 would both be composite\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/7/0e73598fe5c65538c2fdfc5861f717d7700b316d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 \\bmod{30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" />, p±14 would both be composite\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/0/0e0ca4b8e9ec037f32ab69146563fb3e6baab014.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13 \\bmod{30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" />, p±8 would both be composite\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/2/f0208baf75ae1b70fe488d23a5de0c14e41cb24c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17 \\bmod{30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" />, p±8 would both be composite\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/6/83646e3c18f60841d72c9f67089bd1b8a37fa97b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19 \\bmod{30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" />, p±14 would both be composite\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/d/ecd0cc9de38d1d688953525e27fcb3dbefc7fc44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23 \\bmod{30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" />, p±2 would both be composite\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/3/ec3fe8ad1d19775d3956e9b7549c5ca26e66166a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29 \\bmod{30}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"14\" />, p±4 would both be composite\n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> &lt; 30\n</p><p>From here, just try all possible p and find the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/4/a345b78def48f40b66101a7f512627189997f108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {038}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~Mathophobia\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://youtu.be/8_C0lmbpRWA?si=1d1wRlity1w_nHHf\">1984 AIME #14</a>\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://mathproblemsolvingskills.wordpress.com/\">MathProblemSolvingSkills.com</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_using_Bashing\">Video Solution using Bashing</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution using Bashing\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n98zEG1-Hrs\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n98zEG1-Hrs</a>\n~North America Math Contest Go Go Go\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"